KG42.register("rules-b952ef999c63b037007c1d72",{"id":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing::v141-c-R012","paper":"14-stackelberg_pv_sharing","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R012","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M03","name":"Local-area admission","process_stage":"participation","market_meaning":"Eligibility to participate as a player in the Cournot local microgrid market requires seller-role prosumer participation. Scope: Eligibility to be a game player in the Cournot benchmark local market inside a microgrid. Condition: Prosumer participation must be in the seller role.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function admission.local_area under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["admission.local_area","participation.prosumer"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R012-E001","source":"admission.local_area","target":"participation.prosumer","type":"requires","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R012-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E12"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"participation","context_text":"Eligibility to be a game player in the Cournot benchmark local market inside a microgrid.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E12"]},"x":[],"theta":[],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R012-C001","kind":"logical","role":"core","statement":"Eligibility to participate as a player in the Cournot local microgrid market requires seller-role prosumer participation. Scope: Eligibility to be a game player in the Cournot benchmark local market inside a microgrid. Condition: Prosumer participation must be in the seller role.","expression":"\\mathrm{Players}_{\\mathrm{Cournot\\ local\\ market}} \\subseteq \\mathrm{Prosumers}^{\\mathrm{seller\\ role}}","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["admission.local_area","participation.prosumer"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g03-E12"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E12","location":{"location_id":"src-ed046424ff-p10-c1r4__v141-a-M03-pricing","page":10,"printed_page":null,"section":"Appendix B Cournot Model","anchor_text":"the local market inside a microgrid by using the Cournot model. As referring to model of [28]–[30], ","equation_id":"(31)-(32)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-10.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"Cournot model was applied in the electricity market with multiple producers (i.e., power plants). We have reformulated the local market inside a microgrid by using the Cournot model. As referring to model of [28]–[30], the players in the local market are only limited to seller role prosumers, the relation between selling prices and amount of energy is\np_s = a - bE^s. \\quad (31)\nIf E^s = 0, there is no PV energy that can be supplied in the microgrid. Therefore, the selling price should be equal to the price of utility grid \\lambda^b. If E^s \\ge E^b, the selling energy is more than the required energy. Then, the selling price should be minimized to \\lambda^s. Thus, the price function (31) should include the points (0,\\lambda^b) and (E^b,\\lambda^s), and the parameter a and b can be obtained\na = \\lambda^b, \\quad b = (\\lambda^b - \\lambda^s)/E^b. \\quad (32)"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":"This admission rule contains no numeric design or operational decision variable; it is a categorical eligibility condition restricting which role may participate.","empty_theta_reason":"No fixed numeric parameter or coefficient is used in this rule; the only condition is the categorical seller-role restriction on participation."},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"admission.local_area","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g03-E12","quote":"We have reformulated the local market inside a microgrid by using the Cournot model. As referring to model of [28]–[30], the players in the local market are only limited to seller role prosumers"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"2fbaac46c214fcae10bb7a9a16aa7e44e6f07b02862a2225fad0f1ed52345626","applicability":"formalized","reason":"The source explicitly states that the players in the Cournot local market inside a microgrid are limited to seller-role prosumers. This admission restriction is formalized as a set-inclusion condition over the frozen admission-to-participation relation. The B evidence remains unreviewed in this experiment.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R012-C001","node_ids":["admission.local_area","participation.prosumer"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R012-E001"],"rationale":"The formalized admission restriction is exactly the frozen requires edge from admission.local_area to participation.prosumer, with the source's explicit seller-role qualifier applying to the participating prosumers. No additional graph node or edge is needed for the categorical seller-role restriction."}],"revision_requests":[]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
